{"name":"Vagabond","hex":"#aa8877","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vagabond","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person on a trip of indeterminate destination and/or length of time.","One who usually wanders from place to place, having no fixed dwelling, or not abiding in it, and usually without the means of honest livelihood."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roam, as a vagabond"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vagabond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vagabond (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Vagabond (Korean: 배가본드) is a 2019 South Korean television series starring Lee Seung-gi, Bae Suzy and Shin Sung-rok. It aired on SBS TV from September 20 to November 23, 2019, for 16 episodes. Each episode was released on Netflix in South Korea and internationally after their television broadcast."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Vagabond_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vagabond_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Vagabond (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Vagabond  is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Takehiko Inoue. Based on Eiji Yoshikawa's novel Musashi, the story is a fictionalized account of the life of the Japanese swordsman, Miyamoto Musashi. It has been serialized in Kodansha's seinen manga magazine Morning since September 1998, with its chapters collected in 37 tankōbon volumes by July 2014. Viz Media licensed the series for English release in North America and has published the 37 volumes by April 2015. The series has been on indefinite hiatus since May 2015."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/99/Vagabond_%28manga%29_vol._1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vagabond_(manga)"},{"title":"Vagrancy","blocks":[{"text":"Vagrancy is the condition of wandering homelessness without regular employment or income. Vagrants usually live in poverty and support themselves by travelling while engaging in begging, scavenging, or petty theft. In Western countries, vagrancy was historically a crime punishable with forced labor, military service, imprisonment, or confinement to dedicated labor houses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/John_Everett_Millais_-_The_Blind_Girl%2C_1854-56.jpg/330px-John_Everett_Millais_-_The_Blind_Girl%2C_1854-56.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vagrancy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/Takehiko_Inoue_20240312_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/Takehiko_Inoue_20240312_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Manga author Takehiko Inoue wanted to draw a more realistic series through Vagabond","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATakehiko_Inoue_20240312_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Reeve_and_Serfs.jpg/500px-Reeve_and_Serfs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Reeve_and_Serfs.jpg/500px-Reeve_and_Serfs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReeve_and_Serfs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Orsay_Stevens_vagabondage_IMG_9432.jpg/500px-Orsay_Stevens_vagabondage_IMG_9432.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Orsay_Stevens_vagabondage_IMG_9432.jpg/1280px-Orsay_Stevens_vagabondage_IMG_9432.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars